sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: DECISIONS 3 (automatic deploy = Gateway-published native schedule, no POST back), R1-R2, ADR 0244, behavior names by target. Replaces instance.policy_event. docs/reference/deployments.md#automatic-deployments.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 3, 5 (no per-minute Node read: the schedule inputs carry the deployed commit, and the Gateway republishes them on each deploy).
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: instance:auto-deploy:enable · Automatic deploys
  %% kind: instance.auto_deploy
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as app-prod Node<br/>Node 12 over ssh
  CLI->>GW: Enable or disable automatic deployment
  Note over GW: Record the existing Instance switch
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - production retains its existing eligibility and pause contract
  %%> - development requires an active ready container default on an active app-dev Node
  %%> - checkout Instances and clones are never selected for development auto-deploy
  GW-->>CLI: Return the Instance
  alt development container default
    loop enabled minute tick in the Gateway
      GW->>GW: Compare Project head with container seed
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - reuse one remote head read per eligible Project
      %%> - unchanged defaults start no Swamp work
      GW->>GW: Check exact-head green evidence and durable retries
      %%> Rules:
      %%> - re-read the configured check for the exact SHA; missing or pending evidence never deploys
      %%> - retry after ten then twenty minutes; a third failure stops that SHA
      %%> - disabling and enabling keeps failures; manual development deployment resets them
      opt changed eligible head may deploy
        GW->>GW: Recheck selection and admit ordinary instance.deploy
        %%> Rules:
        %%> - recheck the flag, placement, readiness, seed and configured check under the Instance lock
        %%> - a queued, running or waiting Operation holds the Instance
        %%> - record the admitted SHA atomically; no Swamp development checkpoint or policy run
        GW->>SW: Execute the ordinary pinned deployment
        SW->>N: Run the existing container deployment phases
        SW-->>GW: Native terminal result
        GW->>GW: Project the seed and account for the admitted SHA once
      end
    end
  else production Instance
    Note over SW: Existing production policy and independent pause
    SW->>SW: Select the newest eligible green first-parent commit
    opt deploy due
      SW->>N: Execute the existing production deployment
      SW-->>GW: Native terminal result and policy events
    end
  end
